# Living architecture map

Keep this repo's `CLAUDE.md` a **living architecture map** — the standing defense against
re-spending tokens rediscovering how the system works. After any task that required non-trivial
discovery of HOW the system works (which secret / table / Lambda / queue, the deploy path, the auth
model, a load-bearing gotcha that cost time), record the salient map in `CLAUDE.md`'s
*Architecture & operations* section (create it if missing), and put step-by-step procedures in a
`docs/` runbook linked from it.

**Keep it CONCISE — this is the whole point.** `CLAUDE.md` is auto-loaded into every session, so a
bloated map wastes the exact tokens it is meant to save. A tight component map + the gotchas that
cost time, not prose; link to `docs/*` for depth; prune stale/wrong entries when you notice them.
The test for an entry: **would it have saved *this* task's discovery?** If not, leave it out.

Claude Code twin: the global `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` "Living architecture map (ALL repos)" section.
